Parse and validate a message graph: unique node IDs, selectors, typed literals or
connections, existing dependencies, acyclic order, at most 128 nodes.
Each node has receiver input, selector, argument inputs, label and position.
Resolve dependencies deterministically. Execute using the evaluator's typed dispatch.
Retain literal object references and object results in the Wiring object's Array.
Record each successful result and order. On a signal store the failed-node report
and re-signal to the caller. Resume skips successful nodes and retries the failed one.
Reject resuming a changed graph. Completed runs resume without repeating effects.
GET /wiring creates/reuses the main ordinary Wiring object or reads a specified one.
Return its ID, definition and run report; normal interactions perform saves and runs.
